# Page Section Workflow

## Core rule
- Build every screen **section by section**, never a full page in one task.
- For each section: **create the component first**, then use it on the screen.
- Do not start the next section until the user asks for it.

## Live shop.app reference (required)
- Screenshots in `docs/ui-reference/` are **not enough**.
- Before implementing or refining a section, open the matching page on **https://shop.app** in the agent browser (e.g. `/categories` for Categories) and fully inspect that section: layout, spacing, radii, typography, carousel/scroll behavior, and breakpoints.
- User screenshots complement live inspection; they do **not** replace it.

## Current focus
- Active screen: **Categories** (`CategoriesScreen`, route `/categories` ↔ shop.app Explore)
- Categories section order:
  1. App chrome (`AppShell` — already done; skip unless changing nav)
  2. Explore featured (`CategoriesExploreFeaturedSection` — H1 + editorial carousel)
  3. Browse categories
  4. Product rows (Top rated / New in …)
  5. Site footer (`SiteFooter`)
  6. Floating search (when requested)

## Placement
- Reusable pieces: `shared/.../ui/components/`
- App chrome navigation: `shared/.../ui/navigation/`
- Screen-specific sections: `shared/.../ui/sections/categories/`
- Screen assembly: `shared/.../ui/screens/CategoriesScreen.kt`
- Shell: `shared/.../ui/shell/AppShell.kt`, `AppContentContainer.kt`

## Visual reference
- Use `docs/ui-reference/` screenshots for the **active** section **and** live shop.app.
- Match shop.app look with Persian RTL and `VitranTheme`.
- Do **not** use Material3 `NavigationBar` / `NavigationRail` for app chrome.

## When to use
- Always, for any screen/section UI work in this repo.

## When to update
- Active screen changes (e.g. leave Categories for Deals).
- Categories section order changes.
- Package paths for components/screens settle or move.
